# Bank Loan Analytics Dashboard | Power BI

An end-to-end Power BI project analyzing a bank's loan portfolio: funded amount, repayments, good vs bad loans, interest rate and debt-to-income (DTI).



## Business Problem
The bank needs to monitor lending performance, separate good loans from bad loans, and track repayment behavior to make data-driven lending decisions.

## Dataset
- **File:** `data/Financial_loan_data.xlsx`
- **Size:** 38,576 loan applications, 23 columns
- **Period:** January to December 2021
- **Key columns:** ID, ISSUE_DATE, PURPOSE, GRADE, HOME_OWNERSHIP, ADDRESS_STATE, LOAN_STATUS, TERM, DTI, INT_RATE, LOAN_AMOUNT, TOTAL_PAYMENT

## Tools Used
Power BI Desktop, Power Query, DAX

## Loan Classification
| Category | Loan Status | Applications | Share |
|---|---|---|---|
| Good Loan | Fully Paid, Current | 33,243 | 86.18% |
| Bad Loan | Charged Off | 5,333 | 13.82% |

